# Releasing Yuno

Do these in order. Stop after each step until the user says to go on.

1. **Draft.** Write the notes under `## Unreleased` in `CHANGELOG.md`, in the same shape as 1.0.0: the banner, then `### New`, `### Improved`, and `### Miscellaneous`. One or two short lines per change, written for someone using the app. In the same message, say what the version should become and why. A fix on the current release is the next patch (`1.1.1`). New features on the same app are the next minor (`1.1.0`, `1.2.0`). A different app is the next major. `versionCode` in `app/build.gradle.kts` goes up by 1. Show the draft and the version together. Do not bump the version and do not publish. Wait for a yes.
2. **Publish.** Only after they confirm: set `versionName` and `versionCode`, then run `scripts/publish-apk.sh` so the production APK and those notes go to GitHub. Do not install that APK on the phone.

```markdown
## Unreleased

![Yuno](https://github.com/danielkanan/Yuno/raw/main/docs/banner.png?v=2)

### New
- One thing someone would notice.

### Improved
- One thing that already existed and now works better.

### Miscellaneous
- One thing that is neither new nor a fix.
```
